result.competitor:
No BiH or ex-YU vendor of AML or KYC compliance software for small non-financial obliged entities was found. Bosnian/Croatian-language searches covered software, apps, risk-assessment tools and services for accountants and agencies. The results showed:
- UK/US/NZ tools (Credas, Thirdfort, FigsFlow, Xama, AMLHUB, SmartSearch) built for UK and other foreign rules, without BiH forms or language;
- Asseco SEE's AML system, which targets banks;
- consultancy articles (unija.com) and paid seminars (Paragraf).
There is no free state tool for the internal kit (risk assessment, procedures, client file). The FUZIP guides are only guidance. Not checked: whether the FOO has an electronic reporting portal for STRs, and local consultancies that sell document templates.

result.duty:
The duty is current and in force (state law, Sl. glasnik BiH 13/2024, applies across FBiH, RS and Brcko). Art. 5 obliged entities include audit firms, providers of accounting, bookkeeping and tax services, and notaries, lawyers and law firms, but the professions only when they take part in specified financial or property transactions. Under Art. 5(2) real estate intermediaries are covered, rentals only where monthly rent is 20,000 KM or more. Duties are:
- a documented risk assessment, updated at least yearly and sent to the supervisory body (Art. 10);
- internal policies approved by management (Art. 9(3)-(4));
- an authorised person and a deputy (Art. 9(2)(h));
- staff training;
- CDD and beneficial-owner identification, including for transactions of 30,000 KM or more (Art. 12(1)(b));
- record keeping (Art. 9(2)(l));
- suspicious transaction reports to the FOO (Art. 33, 42).
The Council of Ministers adopted the rulebook in early Jan 2026 and published it in early Feb 2026, with 90 days to align internal acts. FUZIP risk-assessment guidelines have been out since April 2026. FUZIP's special inspection programme ran from 28 Sep 2026 to end-2026 and covered bookkeeping, accounting and tax firms, auditors, gambling operators, TCSPs, vehicle and precious-goods dealers and real estate intermediaries. Fines run from 5,000 to 200,000 KM, and 20,000-80,000 KM for no risk analysis or for CDD failures. This is all under a June 2026 FATF action plan. Not checked: the 5-year retention period (Art. 93 and the penalty articles were truncated in the fetch) and supervision of RS and Brcko entities.
